  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Petite Étoile is a brasserie, bar and restaurant at 14 avenue de la 1ère Armée in Draguignan. Its website explains that it works with seasonal produce from a family market gardener, the father of one of the partners, to make tasty, generous dishes. The Dracénie Provence Verdon tourist office page describes traditional home-made French cooking, a warm setting with about 40 covers, a covered terrace and, on summer days, a pleasant terrace. The business has been registered in the Sirene directory since 2022.</p>
      <h2>Opening hours and booking</h2>
      <p>The website announces opening Monday to Friday from 10am to 3pm and from 6:30pm to 1am, closed on Sundays; the Saturday line is hard to read there, and directories give 9:30am to 3pm and 6:30pm to 1am, Monday to Saturday. Bookings on 06 29 31 96 10, the brasserie's number. The tourist office page gives the address as "26 avenue de la 1ère Armée", while the brasserie's website gives number 14.</p>
      <h2>What about dogs?</h2>
      <p>Neither the brasserie's website nor the tourist office page mentions dogs. Some customers say they stopped for lunch with their dog and were warmly welcomed, and a review aggregator lists dogs as allowed both inside and outside: these are testimonials, not a rule set by the restaurant. Nothing is specified about dog size, a water bowl or a supplement.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: call 06 29 31 96 10 before you come to check that your dog can sit with you, inside or on the covered terrace.</div>
      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Draguignan's town centre and its shops are close at hand to extend your outing.</p>
